{
  "markdown": "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n[Heraldic eagle emblem with D·C·O text]\n\n\n🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾🙾\n\n\nVALUE AT MATURITY R 101,800-00 \n[D.C.O. logo] \nDue 21st January 1965 \nBARCLAYS BANK D.C.O. \n(REGISTERED COMMERCIAL BANK) \nWITH WHICH IS AMALGAMATED \nTHE NATIONAL BANK OF SOUTH AFRICA LIMITED \nNo. 301 \n\nHead Office in South Africa\nJOHANNESBURG\n25th. μ\n\n\nNEGOTIABLE CERTIFICATE OF DEPOSIT\nThis certifies that there has been deposited with Barclays Bank D.C.O.\nthe sum of R100,000-00 (One hundred thousand Rand)\npayable to the Bearer of this Certificate the Order of\n\n\n180 days after date hereof together with interest at the rate of \n3.65 per cent per annum. \n\n[SIGNED]\nThe amount of the deposit and the interest thereon will be repaid\nupon presentation of this Certificate at the Johannesburg Branch of\nBarclays Bank D.C.O. on or after\n21st January 1965 on which\ndate interest will cease.\n[ILLEGIBLE_SIGNATURE]\nGeneral Manager\n[ILLEGIBLE_SIGNATURE]\n\n\nTHE ISSUE AND NEGOTIATION OF THIS CERTIFICATE ARE SUBJECT TO THE CONDITIONS PRINTED ON THE\nBACK HEREOF\n* DELETE WHICHEVER IS INAPPLICABLE\n\n\n⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜⚜\n\n\n<figure type=\"ILLUSTRATION\">\n\n<description>The image displays a vertical arrangement of three rectangular postage stamps or labels from South Africa, presented in a black-and-white, high-contrast style. Each stamp features a consistent design: the text 'SOUTH AFRICA' at the top, a central coat of arms emblem, a specific currency value in Rand ('R4', 'R1', and 'R20' respectively), and 'SUID-AFRIKA' at the bottom. The stamps are stacked vertically, with the R4 stamp at the top, the R1 stamp in the middle, and the R20 stamp at the bottom. The background appears to be a document or paper with some faint, possibly handwritten or printed annotations along the left and right edges.</description></figure>\n\nly 1964. \n\n<!-- doc_id=parse-01m3seb3aafj7gcdc6zskdmm9a -->",
